Social Problems
Social problems are challenges that quietly erode the well-being of many and stand against the values a society holds dear.
About
Poverty, unemployment, inequality, discrimination, crime, and corruption grow from economic, cultural, and political roots. Solving them calls for shared awareness, wise policies, and committed action.
This repository is a simple project to describe, organize, and learn about major social problems.
Problems Covered
Problem
Short Description
Poverty
Lack of resources to meet basic needs
Unemployment
Inability to find work despite willingness and skill
Inequality
Unfair gaps in income, opportunity, and access
Discrimination
Unequal treatment based on identity or background
Crime
Acts that harm people and weaken public safety
Corruption
Misuse of power or position for personal gain
Root Causes
Economic
Cultural
Political
Possible Solutions
Shared public awareness and education
Sound, fair government policies
Committed community and individual action
